# 02 - SOC-SIEM and Wazuh Installation

## Objective

Deploy a Wazuh SIEM server to collect, analyze, and alert on security events from homelab endpoints.

## VM Specifications

| Setting | Value |
|---|---|
| Name | SOC-SIEM |
| RAM | 4096 MB |
| CPU | 2 cores |
| Disk | 70 GB |
| Network | Shared Network |
| Hostname | soc-siem |

## Ubuntu Server Installation

1. Boot from Ubuntu Server ARM64 ISO
2. Select English language
3. Choose keyboard layout
4. Select Ubuntu Server installation type
5. Set network to DHCP automatically
6. Set hostname: `soc-siem`
7. Create username and password
8. Enable OpenSSH server
9. Use entire virtual disk, no LVM
10. Complete installation and reboot

## Network Verification

After first boot, verify connectivity:

```bash
ip addr
ping -c 4 8.8.8.8
```

Expected result: IP address assigned, ping succeeds.

## Package Update Troubleshooting

During installation, Ubuntu archive mirror connections over HTTP failed.

**Fix applied:** Changed package sources to HTTPS after installation:

```bash
sudo sed -i 's|http://|https://|g' /etc/apt/sources.list
sudo sed -i 's|http://|https://|g' /etc/apt/sources.list.d/*.sources
sudo apt clean
sudo apt update
sudo apt upgrade -y
```

## Wazuh Installation

Install basic tools:

```bash
sudo apt install -y curl wget git unzip net-tools htop vim ufw
```

Download and run Wazuh installer:

```bash
cd ~
curl -O https://packages.wazuh.com/4.x/wazuh-install.sh
sudo bash ./wazuh-install.sh -a
```

**Important:** Save the dashboard credentials displayed at installation completion.

## Dashboard Access

From macOS host browser:

```text
https://192.168.64.9
```

Accept the self-signed certificate warning.

## Verification

| Check | Method |
|---|---|
| Wazuh manager running | `sudo systemctl status wazuh-manager` |
| Wazuh indexer running | `sudo systemctl status wazuh-indexer` |
| Wazuh dashboard running | `sudo systemctl status wazuh-dashboard` |
| Dashboard accessible | Browser login successful |

## Troubleshooting

| Problem | Solution |
|---|---|
| Certificate warning | Normal for lab; accept and proceed |
| Installer script not found | Re-run curl download command |
| Service fails to start | Check disk space with `df -h` |

